**issue (bug_risk):** Framebuffer color buffer should be a pipe_surface*, not a stack-allocated struct

`fb.cbufs[]` is an array of `struct pipe_surface *`, but `surf_templ` is a by-value `struct pipe_surface` on the stack. Assigning it directly to `fb.cbufs[0]` won’t compile (and would be invalid even if it did). You need to create a `pipe_surface *` from `surf_templ`, store that pointer in `fb.cbufs[0]`, and later destroy it, e.g.:

```c
struct pipe_surface *surf = pipe->create_surface(pipe, rt, &surf_templ);
if (!surf) { ... }

fb.cbufs[0] = surf;
pipe->set_framebuffer_state(pipe, &fb);

...
pipe->surface_destroy(pipe, surf);
```

This also ensures correct lifetime management via refcounting.
